{"ts": 0.054055, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[90m─\u001b[0m \u001b[93mshelltutor\u001b[0m \u001b[90m─\u001b[0m \u001b[90mStage 4 · Commands, streams, composition\u001b[0m \u001b[90m───────────\u001b[0m \u001b[90m○\u001b[0m\u001b[90m○\u001b[0m\u001b[90m○\u001b[0m\u001b[93m◉\u001b[0m\u001b[90m○\u001b[0m  \u001b[93m4.1\u001b[0m \u001b[90m─\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 229}
{"ts": 0.05408, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\r\n", "len": 2}
{"ts": 0.05573, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[1;97m4.1 — reading a command\u001b[0m\r\n\r\nA shell command has a small grammar:\r\n  \u001b[36mcommand  options  arguments\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n  \u001b[92mls -l /etc\u001b[0m               \u001b[90m# option + argument\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[92mwc -l poem.txt\u001b[0m           \u001b[90m# count lines in a file\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[92mecho \"hello world\"\u001b[0m       \u001b[90m# an argument with a space — quoted\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[91mSpaces matter.\u001b[0m  The shell splits on spaces; \u001b[36mquote\u001b[0m a name that has one:\r\n  \u001b[92mvim \"my notes.txt\"\u001b[0m       \u001b[90m# opens one file\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[92mvim my notes.txt\u001b[0m         \u001b[90m# opens TWO files: 'my' and 'notes.txt'\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[36mcommand -v\u001b[0m asks the shell whether a command exists:\r\n  \u001b[92mcommand -v ls\u001b[0m            \u001b[90m# prints the path; exits 0\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[92mcommand -v vim\u001b[0m           \u001b[90m# does Vim exist on this system?\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[93m▶ Try a few \u001b[92mcommand -v\u001b[93m probes, then \u001b[92mnext\u001b[93m.\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 873}
{"ts": 0.056129, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 251}
