{"ts": 0.080877, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[90m─\u001b[0m \u001b[93mshelltutor\u001b[0m \u001b[90m─\u001b[0m \u001b[90mStage 4 · Commands, streams, composition\u001b[0m \u001b[90m───────────\u001b[0m \u001b[90m○\u001b[0m\u001b[90m○\u001b[0m\u001b[90m○\u001b[0m\u001b[93m◉\u001b[0m\u001b[90m○\u001b[0m  \u001b[93m4.2\u001b[0m \u001b[90m─\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 229}
{"ts": 0.080911, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\r\n", "len": 2}
{"ts": 0.082463, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[1;97m4.2 — the pipe\u001b[0m\r\n\r\nA \u001b[36mpipe\u001b[0m ( \u001b[92m|\u001b[0m ) sends one command's output into the next command's\r\ninput. \u001b[91mMost important idea in the shell.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[92mwc\u001b[0m counts \u001b[36mwhatever you piped in\u001b[0m:\r\n  \u001b[92mwc -l poem.txt\u001b[0m          \u001b[90m# lines in poem.txt\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[92mseq 1 100 | wc -l\u001b[0m       \u001b[90m# 100\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[92mls /usr/bin | wc -l\u001b[0m     \u001b[90m# how many programs are installed\u001b[0m\r\n\r\nPipes stack:\r\n  \u001b[92mls /usr/bin | sort | head\u001b[0m        \u001b[90m# list → sort → first 10\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[92mls /usr/bin | grep ^a\u001b[0m            \u001b[90m# names starting with 'a'\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[92mls /usr/bin | grep ^a | wc -l\u001b[0m    \u001b[90m# …and count them\u001b[0m\r\n\r\nEach piece is a normal command; only the connector is new. \u001b[92m|\u001b[0m is Shift+Backslash.\r\n\r\n\u001b[93m▶ Try a few pipelines, then \u001b[92mnext\u001b[93m.\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 818}
{"ts": 0.082836, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 251}
